{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall command. Pure.</b> Without dregs, as we learned in Menachot: they pick from the top of the olive, etc." "<b>Beaten.</b> He crushes the olives in a mortar and does not grind them in a mill, so that there be no dregs in it; and after he has brought out the first drop, he puts them into the mill and grinds them. And the second oil is disqualified for the Menorah but fit for meal-offerings, for it says ״כָּתִית לַמָּאוֹר״ — beaten for the luminary — and not beaten for meal-offerings (Menachot 6)." "<b>To cause the lamp to burn continually.</b> He kindles it until the flame goes up of itself (Shabbat 21)." "<b>Continually.</b> Every night and night is called תָּמִיד, as you say ״עֹלַת תָּמִיד״ — and it is only from day to day; and so with the meal-offering of flat-cakes תָּמִיד is stated, and it is only half in the morning and half in the evening; but the תָּמִיד stated regarding the showbread is from sabbath to sabbath."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:02.142075538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}